Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------

Every file inherited from the upstream project has been modified. The
substantive changes are:

  * The CLI adapter layer (`scripts/lib/grok.mjs`) was replaced by
    `scripts/lib/cursor.mjs`, which drives the Cursor CLI (`cursor-agent`)
    instead of the Grok Build CLI (`grok`).
  * Working-directory selection moved from `--cwd` to `--workspace`.
  * Read-only execution moved from `--sandbox read-only` (a sandbox profile
    that is not enforced on Windows) to Cursor's `--mode ask` / `--mode plan`
    execution modes.
  * Headless runs now pass `--trust`, because a headless Cursor run otherwise
    stops on the workspace-trust prompt.
  * The reasoning-effort flag (`--effort`) was removed; Cursor carries effort
    in the model id instead (for example `gpt-5.6-sol-xhigh`).
  * Structured output no longer uses a `--json-schema` flag, which Cursor does
    not have; the schema is supplied in the prompt and the response envelope
    from `--output-format json` is unwrapped before parsing.
  * Session ids are read back from Cursor's result envelope rather than being
    assigned before the run.
  * The Claude-session import command (`grok import`) and its supporting module
    were removed; the Cursor CLI has no equivalent.
  * The authentication probe uses `cursor-agent status` (and `CURSOR_API_KEY` /
    `CURSOR_AUTH_TOKEN`) rather than a models probe.
  * Binary override renamed from `GROK_BINARY` to `CURSOR_AGENT_BINARY`, and
    the session environment variable from `GROK_CC_SESSION_ID` to
    `CURSOR_CC_SESSION_ID`.
  * All command, agent, skill, and marketplace identifiers were renamed from
    `grok-build` to `cursor-cc`.

